# Fixing PipeWire Audio on Void Linux (KDE Plasma / Non-Systemd)

This guide documents how to set up and troubleshoot **PipeWire**, **WirePlumber**, and **pipewire-pulse** on **Void Linux**, including workarounds for missing ALSA SPA plugins and `RTKit` / `RLIMIT_RTTIME` `SIGKILL` crashes in PipeWire `1.6.10`.

---

## 1. Install Required Packages

Install PipeWire, WirePlumber, PulseAudio compatibility, ALSA integration, and the SPA hardware plugins (`libspa-alsa` is required for sound card detection):

```bash
sudo xbps-install -S pipewire wireplumber pipewire-pulse alsa-pipewire libspa-alsa libspa-bluetooth
```

### Link ALSA Configuration
Route standard ALSA applications through PipeWire:

```bash
sudo mkdir -p /etc/alsa/conf.d
sudo ln -sf /usr/share/alsa/alsa.conf.d/50-pipewire.conf /etc/alsa/conf.d/
sudo ln -sf /usr/share/alsa/alsa.conf.d/99-pipewire-default.conf /etc/alsa/conf.d/
```

---

## 2. Configure PipeWire to Launch WirePlumber & PipeWire-Pulse

On Void Linux, starting `pipewire` alone can automatically spawn `wireplumber` and `pipewire-pulse` via drop-in configs in `~/.config/pipewire/pipewire.conf.d/`:

```bash
mkdir -p ~/.config/pipewire/pipewire.conf.d

ln -sf /usr/share/examples/pipewire/10-wireplumber.conf ~/.config/pipewire/pipewire.conf.d/
ln -sf /usr/share/examples/pipewire/20-pipewire-pulse.conf ~/.config/pipewire/pipewire.conf.d/
```

*(Note: If those example files are in `/usr/share/pipewire/pipewire.conf.d/` on your system, link from there instead.)*

---

## 3. Fix `SIGKILL` / `RLIMIT_RTTIME` & D-Bus Assertion Crashes

### Problem
On non-systemd distributions like Void Linux:
1. When `rtkit` grants realtime (`SCHED_RR`) priority to PipeWire threads, the Linux kernel enforces a strict `RLIMIT_RTTIME` watchdog. When opening an audio stream or switching sinks, PipeWire can exceed this limit and get silently killed (`SIGKILL`) by the kernel with no `dmesg` output.
2. Setting `rtkit.enabled = false` in PipeWire `1.6.10` triggers a D-Bus assertion crash (`assertion "path != NULL" failed` in `dbus_message_new_method_call`).

### Solution
Disable `module-rt` cleanly in both `pipewire.conf.d` and `pipewire-pulse.conf.d` so PipeWire avoids `RLIMIT_RTTIME` kills and the `module-rt` D-Bus bug:

```bash
mkdir -p ~/.config/pipewire/pipewire.conf.d ~/.config/pipewire/pipewire-pulse.conf.d

cat << 'EOF' > ~/.config/pipewire/pipewire.conf.d/10-rt.conf
context.properties = {
    module.rt = false
}
EOF

cp ~/.config/pipewire/pipewire.conf.d/10-rt.conf ~/.config/pipewire/pipewire-pulse.conf.d/10-rt.conf
```

*(Alternative: If you want to keep `module-rt` loaded without realtime threads, set `rt.prio = 0` inside `libpipewire-module-rt` args instead.)*

---

## 4. Autostart on Login (KDE Plasma / Desktop Environments)

Enable XDG autostart for `pipewire.desktop` **only** (since `pipewire` spawns `wireplumber` and `pipewire-pulse` via the configs from Step 2):

```bash
mkdir -p ~/.config/autostart
ln -sf /usr/share/applications/pipewire.desktop ~/.config/autostart/
```

> **Warning:** Do **not** also symlink `wireplumber.desktop` or `pipewire-pulse.desktop` into `~/.config/autostart/`, or duplicate instances will collide over `/run/user/$UID/pipewire-0` and `/run/user/$UID/pulse/native`.

---

## 5. Restart & Verify Audio

### Clean Restart
Stop any leftover instances, clear stale sockets, and start PipeWire:

```bash
pkill -u "\$USER" -x 'pipewire|wireplumber'
rm -f "/run/user/(id -u)/pulse/native" "/run/user/(id -u)"/pipewire-0*
pipewire &
```

### Check Devices & Set Default Output
List detected sinks and sources:

```bash
wpctl status
```

Set your preferred output device (replace `<SINK_ID>` with the numeric ID listed under **Audio -> Sinks**):

```bash
wpctl set-default <SINK_ID>
```

### Test Playback
Verify left and right audio channels:

```bash
speaker-test -c 2 -t wav -l 1
```
